    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d281">

                <pb facs="0438" n="350" sameAs="frus:frus1892/pg350"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Foster to Baron
                            Fava.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1892-07-21"><hi rendition="#italic">July 21,
                        1892</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Dear Baron Fava</hi>: In pursuance of my promise made
                    in our conversation of this morning, I have much pleasure in handing you a copy
                    of the telegram sent to-day by the President to His Majesty King Humbert. This
                    whole episode, reflecting as it does the cordial sentiments of two friendly
                    peoples, has been most gratifying to me.</p>
                <p>I am, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">John W. Foster.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
